  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The conductor has several prepared pieces and can assign time blocks without changing the booked start or finish time.\", \"decision\": \"How should the order of rehearsal pieces be set?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe choir sings brief extracts from the prepared pieces at the start, and the conductor then sets the remaining sequence. The order responds to how the group sounds that day rather than relying entirely on earlier expectations.\nThe conductor asks section leaders which prepared pieces need attention and then publishes a balanced rehearsal sequence. Reports from different voice parts shape the order before the full choir spends time on the selected difficulties.\nThe conductor orders the pieces by their current musical needs and publishes the sequence before rehearsal. Singers can see which challenges will receive attention and prepare their scores before each planned block begins."
    }
  ],
